  "evidence_schema": {
    "child_report": "Native pointer-free static-zero envelope with fixed magic/sizeof; raw .child.bin retained separately. Bounded reporting-width assertions and native round-trip checks preserve actual types; no specific dev_t/ino_t/nlink_t width is assumed. Resolve exact scalar/layout widths from new retained target preflight evidence before runtime. JSON retains every populated callback/native/query cell, every public six-slot event array and all custody/cleanup values. No body claims its own completed report write.",
    "integer_policy": "Native dev_t/ino_t/uid_t/nlink_t/mode_t/off_t fields are compared in their native types first, then checked for lossless uintmax_t/intmax_t reporting. Size values are nonnegative when present.",
    "preexec_scope": "The successful allowlist boolean covers the actual child-side pre-exec close sweep and post-exec verification. Individual pre-exec close/fcntl/exec preparation outcomes are not separate retained native receipts; failures terminate as infrastructure before engine entry.",
